<title>NETHERLANDS: Gist-Brocades sees lower 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Gist-Brocades sees lower 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>DELFT, Netherlands 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch biochemicals and food group Gist-Brocades NV said on Tuesday it expected slightly lower earnings in 1997 comapred to those in 1996.  </p>
<p>&quot;Profits for 1997 will show a slight decrease compared to those of 1996.&quot; Gist said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company reported a 1996 net profit of 158.5 million guilders.</p>
<p>It said that prices of penicillin on the world market had hit an &quot;historic low&quot; -- around half the average price of recent years -- due to additional capacity coming on stream mainly in China and India. This was &quot;a fall greater than forecasts had anticipated,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>Its activities in baking ingredients and food were running fully according to expectations, Gist added.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
